From 2717fb2dd02bcd78bb2181af18a8593a4968164e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <c@example.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 08:18:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/89] Pause the Discord presence instead of removing it

Pausing a song cleared the activity outright, so the card vanished from your
profile and came back on resume. It now stays up with its timestamps dropped.

Timestamps are the whole of it: Discord derives the progress bar from start and
end and nothing else, so a paused track has to send neither - left in place the
bar would carry on advancing as though the song were still playing, which is
worse than no bar at all. The small-image hover text says Paused so the card
reads as stopped rather than as a bar that has quietly stalled.

stopActivity is now reached only when there is no current track at all, which is
the one case with genuinely nothing to describe. The playWhenReady test is kept
rather than isPlaying, for the same reason it was chosen originally: isPlaying
also goes false while a track buffers, and treating that as a pause made the
card flicker on every skip.
