Subject: [PATCH 57/89] Center the navigation rail and remove its logo header

The rail's own logo header anchored the item group to the top, and
Modifier.verticalScroll() on the rail meant weight()-based centering
inside it wouldn't have worked anyway - a scrollable container's
content is measured with unbounded height, so weight has nothing
finite to divide.

Removed the header and the scroll modifier (a handful of nav items
was never going to need scrolling), then centered the item group with
a Spacer(weight(1f)) on each side of it, now that the rail's own
column has a bounded height to distribute.

The unrelated logo toggle on the home tab's own top bar (Settings ->
Appearance, beside the search icon) is untouched - this is only the
Home/Explore/Library side rail.
