From ea63bd49d59fa8d0b42d28013244f6b721ad0aa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:46:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 79/89] EQ visual overhaul + lyrics sync fix + miniplayer
 dismiss fix

- Lyrics: findCurrentLineIndex no longer wraps a transient negative
  playback position into a huge unsigned value, which was snapping the
  highlighted line to the end of the song on some devices/timings.
- Player: swiping the mini player away now collapses back to it instead
  of calling softKillPlayer() (clearMediaItems + deInitQueue), which read
  as the swipe closing the app.
- EQ panel: bigger, full-width drag handle; the panel's own root now
  consumes vertical drags so they no longer fall through to the player's
  BottomSheet and collapse it to the mini player.
- RotaryDial: redesigned as a flat disc with a progress arc and a face
  pointer instead of a bare arc-fill ring; added a centeredAt option for
  boost/cut controls (balance, bass/treble, per-band gain) so 0 shows no
  arc instead of a permanent half-full ring.
- Value-color gradient changed from green-to-red to blue-green-yellow.
- Compressor section now respects the dial/slider toggle (previously
  hardcoded to sliders); band strip now always uses sliders regardless of
  the toggle, matching the reference layout.
- Selected band now gets a bordered box around its frequency label
  instead of just recoloring the text; mini transport uses the Material
  accent color and is ~25% larger; export/import/save/revert buttons and
  the filter-type segmented button now follow the panel's color scheme
  instead of the default Material button colors.
- LiquidBackground rewritten from three soft alpha blobs into a
  ferrofluid-style silhouette (dark glossy blob with a spike crown that
  grows with bass/treble/transients) so it's actually visible against the
  player surface instead of blending into it.
