From 16024a9fc8859ea7307ce50080af57ae7d2f3e99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:44:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Show seek back/forward in a custom layout even with the
 setting off

A custom layout that explicitly asks for BlockId.SEEK_BACKWARD/
SEEK_FORWARD by name was still hidden if the unrelated "seek increment"
setting (Settings -> Player, defaults off) hadn't also been turned on -
so a button deliberately placed via the layout editor just silently
didn't appear, reading as "the layout doesn't work" rather than
"seeking needs its own separate setting enabled too". Falls back to a
plain 10s jump instead of hiding, so it's never a no-op button once
someone has gone to the trouble of adding it.

The stock, unmodified five-button controls row is untouched: it still
hides these two entirely when the setting is off, exactly as before -
this only changes the granular per-block path a custom layout uses.
